A||||45||AkursedX||Survey:  what is everyone's favorite motor?||||1||
Z||000000||AkursedX||06-26-2001||03:50 PM||||I figure this could be an interesting topic to post.  <P>So, what is everyone's favorite motor of all time.  I'm just not talking about ones that fit in a Fiero either.<P>My personal favorite (Well I have 2 actually)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P6250061.JPG"> <BR>The 426 Hemi motor.  It amazes me that even with it being around 30-years old, it is still held in such high regards, and it can produce such great power!<P>As for my other favorite, it has to be the Mazda rotaries.  I absolutley love the smoothness and the high revs that a well maintianed RX-7 makes.  I just wish I understood it better, then I could actually buy one!  I mean I understand the internal of it, but not good enough to become a skilled mechanic on it.<P>So, how about everyone else?  What's you fav?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||06-26-2001||03:57 PM||||Maybe Im old fashioned but I like the original Saturn motor<P>you know, the one they put 5 of in the Saturn 5 first stage, back in '69.<P> now that baby had some HP - and when you got all five lit off, the WFO sound was deep and resonate.<P>  really impressed the babes - nobody could touch you with one of them behind you.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||06-26-2001||04:10 PM||||The 3.8 in my 89 Buick Park Avenue. I changed oil, filters, air filters and the plugs at 100,000. Havn't even had to change the wires. Still runs really strong and has never failed. My older son had the car for a year and a half and now with 140,000 on it the younger boy has it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||06-26-2001||04:11 PM||||BTW you dont need to be a mechanic to drive a wankel - it goes and goes and goes forever!<P> awesome machines - something is really askew to have kept them out of american cars. (they were invented here too, right?!)||||reg||1
Z||000004||WampusCat||06-26-2001||04:21 PM||||Rolls-Royce Pegasus F402-RR-408.  I kinda like those Honda motorcycle V4's too, had a V65 magna and a VFR750 at different times when I wuz a young man.||||reg||6
Z||000005||AkursedX||06-26-2001||04:25 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>BTW you dont need to be a mechanic to drive a wankel - it goes and goes and goes forever!<P> awesome machines - something is really askew to have kept them out of american cars. (they were invented here too, right?!)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The non-turbo one's definitely can go on forever!  They are quite reliable.  But the turbo ones are alot more subject to failure.  The seals have trouble handling the boost. And then there are the twin-turbo 3rd gen RX-7's, I have heard plenty of horror stories about those cars (as far as stock cars)  But if you get a good professionally built motor, they can be quite powerful and reliable.<P>And I think they were developed here in America.  If I remember correctly, rotaries were put in Military jeeps quite some time ago.  But besides that, the domestics shyed away from the design.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Loki||06-26-2001||04:37 PM||||Wankel? Hmmm  When there good there good, and when something even small goes bad  there BAAAAD!!!!!   To tempromental (sp?)<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||06-26-2001||04:54 PM||||Jaguar 4.2L L6.<BR>I love that motor. Sounds *nasty*  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>If I could shoe-horn it into my Fiero, I would in a heartbeat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Next runner up is the Wankel. DARE TO BE DIFFERENT!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||saleenfiero||06-26-2001||04:55 PM||||Bugatti quad turbo W18 or W16.  1001 horse from the factory.  Although I don't think parts are available from Sears for this baby.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Steve Normington||06-26-2001||05:25 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mach10:<BR><B>Jaguar 4.2L L6.<BR>I love that motor. Sounds *nasty*</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sounds really good at 95+ mph in a DHC. Did you know that the British used that motor in an armored car? I believe it was called a Fox or Ferret.<P>Toyota 22RE. That's the engine in my truck that has been driving me to junkyards, part stores, hardware stores, back to the junkyard, to a different part store, back to the first part store, etc.<p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
