Z||000031||84Bill||06-27-2001||08:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B> [QUOTE]Originally posted by AkursedX:<BR>[b] Ahh yes, that is one very pretty sound!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>I wonder if there could be a way to shoehorn one of those into a Fiero??  lol!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> think that V-12 was also used in Supermarine Spitfire and Hawker Sea Fury.<P>[/B][/QUOTE]<BR>They even sound nice in the unlimited hydroplane boats. Something about the sound of those engines, even at idle they have a nice smooth rumble to them.<P><A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/sounds/LOL.wav" TARGET=_blank>LOL</A> I think that engine is as long as a Fiero is wide  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||14
Z||000032||AusFiero||06-27-2001||09:32 AM||||I would have to say the Victa 2 stroke lawnmower engine in my lawnmower mans lawnmower. Makes me smile whenever I hear it because I know it isn't me out there doing it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But other than that I drove a 1973ish model Ferrari with a quad cam v8 with 4 webber carbies on it. Haven't hear a sweeter engine since and I have driven Lamborghinis, Porsches, Lotuses and a lot more. It just sounded so throaty and roaring to go.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000033||Formula88||06-27-2001||09:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>Maybe Im old fashioned but I like the original Saturn motor<P>you know, the one they put 5 of in the Saturn 5 first stage, back in '69.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That would be the Saturn F1 engine, if memory serves.  A cluster of 5 of them made the Saturn V stage 1.  1.5M lbs of thrust - EACH, for a total of 7.5M lbs thrust at liftoff.  BTW, did you know the Saturn V was a diesel?  Yup.  It burned kerosene instead of Hydrogen (that's why the flame is so yellow).  So, that's not too far removed from diesel fuel.  Both the 2nd and 3rd stages used Hydrogen/Oxygen.  <P>Also, the Space Shuttle's main engines, much smaller (each one can fit in the back of a pickup truck - hmmmm) and the cluster of 3 puts out a total of 1.5M lbs thrust.  However, each SRB (solid rocket booster) puts out 3M lbs, so the Space Shuttle has the SAME THRUST on liftoff as the old Saturn V, but it's much lighter.  That explains why the Saturn V just lumbered off the pad and the Shuttle fairly well jumps.<P>Of course, the Titan IV is the hot rod of US space vehicles.  I don't know the specs, but it'll blow the payload bay doors off a shuttle.  I watched the Mars Observer launch on one and was amazed at how fast it accelerated.<P>Now, for my favorite motor - any electric will so.  Engines, on the other hand...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I have to love the Pontiac 428HO, the 455HO (god I miss my 72 Trans Am), and of course the 455SD.  For exotic, the LT5 is awesome, but a new LS6 slightly tweaked can match it's output.  Technology - the great equalizer!<P>And of course, any Ferrari and Lamborghini 12 cylinder.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  How can you not love that sound?||||reg||6
Z||000034||Tigger||06-27-2001||09:58 AM||||Maniak84 and I agree, our favorite is the 2.5L 4-cylinder "duke!"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000035||AkursedX||06-27-2001||03:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR>[B] <BR>Now, for my favorite motor - any electric will so.  Engines, on the other hand...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hehehe, I was waiting for someone to make that comment!<P><BR>WOO HOO!!!!  I finally created a post that got the little flame thing by it!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  My life is now complete!<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic.jpg"> ||||reg||1
